ks at all: of `[checks].probe`, a cheap command run once inside `[checks].probe_timeout_s` (required with it; exit 0 means yes, anything else or the bound is an environment refusal), or, for a tenant that declares no probe, by running `[checks].command` whole (exit 2 means no). The feed says \"checking this machine can run the checks\" before and the answer after. `[checks].command` is what is fast and decisive at the gate; what the forge runs as its own required check need not be run twice. The adapter is given one test command, `attavo test N` (`ATTAVO_TEST_COMMAND`, with `ATTAVO_TEST_TIMEOUT_S` when the tenant declares `[tests].call_timeout_s`), not the checks: it selects, through `[tests].select`, for every path the item has changed since it left the default branch, committed or not (the records directory aside), runs them through `[tests].run`, exits as the run does, and at the bound ends the run with everything it started and exits 124. A selector that maps a path it does not know to nothing hides the tests that would have caught the change; a tenant's selector should send such a path to the whole suite. A `question` from the adapter halts the loop at once (exit 3); nothing answers it in Phase 2. Every run writes the next `build-NN.json`, with the adapter's transcript beside it as `build-NN.log`. Nothing dispatches build; it is typed by the operator. The full contract is in the Phase 2 issue.\n\n## Layout\n\n- `bin/attavo` — the command: `doctor`, `spec-gate`, `approve`, `approval-status`, `build`.\n- `schema/manifest.schema.json` — the shape of a tenant's `attavo.toml`.\n- `schema/records/` — the shape of each stage's record.\n- `adapters/` — the adapter contract (`adapters/README.md`) and two adapters: `claude-code` and `fixture`.\n- `action.yml` — pins Attavo at a tag and puts `attavo` on `PATH`.\n- `templates/workflows/` — three workflows a tenant copies into its own repository (spec-gate, approve, coherence); nothing here is vendored or run by this one. The coherence job mints and signs the attestation on the merge group, against the commit that lands — no attestation record is ever written to the tree; the signed statement lives in the forge's attestation store.\n- `tests/` — the doctor's proofs and the spec and build contracts' rejection tests, with their fixtures under `tests/fixtures/`.\n\nThis repository contains no tenant name, path, or command string.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
