{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L6ZCPrh4QoWnuR6tvGe3AM","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (53.8KB). Full output saved to: /Users/davidbean/.claude/projects/-Users-davidbean-Projects-attavo-worktree-219/0dd7ed4f-100c-4188-9a34-077aa0b6aa25/tool-results/bzmapq88o.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\n     1\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\n     2\t\"\"\"adapters/claude-code/run -- see README.md (this directory) for the four\n     3\tconfiguration keys, and ../README.md for the shared adapter contract.\n     4\t\n     5\tA live `claude` invocation is not exercised by the test suite (judgment\n     6\tis measured, not tested); its argument construction is checked by\n     7\tATTAVO_ADAPTER_DRY_RUN=1, which prints the `claude` command line as a\n     8\tJSON array instead of running it, its response handling is checked by\n     9\tATTAVO_ADAPTER_RESPONSE_FILE, which reads a canned final report object\n    10\tfrom a file instead of invoking `claude`, and (issue #26) its\n    11\t`--output-format stream-json --verbose` mapping -- the event stream\n    12\tthis adapter maps to ATTAVO_EVENTS, and the terminal \"result\" line it\n    13\treads the report object from -- is checked by ATTAVO_ADAPTER_STREAM_FILE,\n    14\twhich feeds a recorded transcript instead.\n    15\t\n    16\tThe whole result is printed to stdout before this adapter's own final\n    17\tline, so build-NN.log carries it as the transcript -- a halt otherwise\n    18\tcannot be explained after the fact. is_error or an absent\n    19\tstructured_output exit 1 on either stage; a build status \"question\"\n    20\twhose question is missing or under MIN_QUESTION_CHARS characters also\n    21\texits 1 (build records the attempt as failed) rather than a halt\n    22\tsomeone must rule on.\n    23\t\n    24\tATTAVO_STAGE=verify branches to a different objective, schema, and\n    25\treport shape (issue #46): the instruction states the verify objective\n    26\t(see verify_instruction) instead of the build one, --json-schema is\n    27\tVERIFY_SCHEMA instead of STATUS_SCHEMA, and the final line carries\n    28\tfindings and tests_named instead of status and question.\n    29\t\n    30\tIssue #78: the boundary is the tool's own sandbox, not a curated\n    31\tallowed_tools list judged per sub-command -- confirmed live (recorded on\n...\n</persisted-output>","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0dd7ed4f-100c-4188-9a34-077aa0b6aa25","uuid":"a6c377d2-9a08-4d6b-bb57-a6c25d8ba429","timestamp":"2026-09-26T02:14:08.935Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"     1\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\n     2\t\"\"\"adapters/claude-code/run -- see README.md (this directory) for the four\n     3\tconfiguration keys, and ../README.md for the shared adapter contract.\n     4\t\n     5\tA live `claude` invocation is not exercised by the test suite (judgment\n     6\tis measured, not tested); its argument construction is checked by\n     7\tATTAVO_ADAPTER_DRY_RUN=1, which prints the `claude` command line as a\n     8\tJSON array instead of running it, its response handling is checked by\n     9\tATTAVO_ADAPTER_RESPONSE_FILE, which reads a canned final report object\n    10\tfrom a file instead of invoking `claude`, and (issue #26) its\n    11\t`--output-format stream-json --verbose` mapping -- the event stream\n    12\tthis adapter maps to ATTAVO_EVENTS, and the terminal \"result\" line it\n    13\treads the report object from -- is checked by ATTAVO_ADAPTER_STREAM_FILE,\n    14\twhich feeds a recorded transcript instead.\n    15\t\n    16\tThe whole result is printed to stdout before this adapter's own final\n    17\tline, so build-NN.log carries it as the transcript -- a halt otherwise\n    18\tcannot be explained after the fact. is_error or an absent\n    19\tstructured_output exit 1 on either stage; a build status \"question\"\n    20\twhose question is missing or under MIN_QUESTION_CHARS characters also\n    21\texits 1 (build records the attempt as failed) rather than a halt\n    22\tsomeone must rule on.\n    23\t\n    24\tATTAVO_STAGE=verify branches to a different objective, schema, and\n    25\treport shape (issue #46): the instruction states the verify objective\n    26\t(see verify_instruction) instead of the build one, --json-schema is\n    27\tVERIFY_SCHEMA instead of STATUS_SCHEMA, and the final line carries\n    28\tfindings and tests_named instead of status and question.\n    29\t\n    30\tIssue #78: the boundary is the tool's own sandbox, not a curated\n    31\tallowed_tools list judged per sub-command -- confirmed live (recorded on\n    32\tthe issue, 2026-09-10) against `claude 2.1.268`: `--settings` carrying\n    33\t`{\"sandbox\": {\"enabled\": true, \"allowUnsandboxedCommands\": false}}` under\n    34\t`-p` refuses a write outside the working directory (\"operation not\n    35\tpermitted\") and, with `network.allowedDomains: []`, refuses an outbound\n    36\tconnection (\"deny network-outbound ...\"), both before `--allowedTools`\n    37\tis ever consulted. build's `--settings` therefore enables the sandbox and\n    38\tforbids the unsandboxed fallback; verify's additionally sets\n    39\t`filesystem.denyWrite` on the working directory itself (confirmed live:\n    40\t`denyWrite` takes a list of paths, not a bare boolean -- `true` alone did\n    41\tnot stop a write inside the directory). `--allowedTools` shrinks to the\n    42\ttool names each stage may use at all -- `Read,Edit,Write,Bash` for build,\n    43\t`Read,Bash` for verify -- since Edit and Write are not Bash and the\n    44\tsandbox does not govern them. `allowed_tools` is retired as a manifest\n    45\tkey: a config that still declares it is refused by name rather than\n    46\tsilently accepted.\n    47\t\n    48\tIssue #88 (class A: a report is not a question). `--json-schema`\n    49\tconstrains the tool's structured_output to \"done\"/\"question\", but\n    50\tnothing stops \"question\" from carrying a status report rather than an\n    51\tactual question -- confirmed against tenant zero's own corpus, five\n    52\tspecimens with no \"?\" anywhere in the text. A \"question\" whose text\n    53\tclears MIN_QUESTION_CHARS but contains no \"?\" is a report, not a\n    54\tquestion: this adapter re-invokes the executor once, appending\n    55\tREINSTRUCTION to the same instruction, before ever reporting a halt to\n    56\ta person. A second report in a row still halts (someone must look), but\n    57\tits report line carries \"class\": \"non-question\" and both raw results\n    58\treached stdout above it -- an extra field bin/attavo's own record schema\n    59\tdoes not know about and never has to: it reads \"status\"/\"question\" off\n    60\tthis line exactly as before, so a \"question\" halt still halts. Read via\n    61\tATTAVO_ADAPTER_RESPONSE_FILE, a JSON array is a queue -- one canned\n    62\tresult per invocation this adapter makes, its last element repeating\n    63\tonce exhausted -- while a single object still repeats for every call,\n    64\tunchanged.\n    65\t\n    66\tIssue #88 (class B: work that outlives the invocation). Confirmed live,\n    67\tthis machine, `claude 2.1.269`: with both \"Agent\" and \"Task\" allowed, a\n    68\tprompt asking for a subagent produced `subagent_stats.spawned: 1`, `\"Agent\"`\n    69\talone in `--disallowedTools` (Task is not a distinct tool in this build)\n    70\tbrought it back to 0 -- the tool's own reply named \"Workflow\" as the\n    71\tother path to background work, so both are named here. `--allowedTools`\n    72\tis an allow-list a background spawn does not consult (tenant zero's\n    73\tspecimen: `--allowedTools` without \"Agent\" or \"Workflow\" in it at all did\n    74\tnot stop three of them), so this adapter also disallows them by name on\n    75\tboth stages and, after the run, refuses by name -- exit 1, not a\n    76\thalt -- any response whose subagent_stats.spawned is not zero, with the\n    77\tcounts in the message. A tool that reports no subagent_stats at all\n    78\t(spawned absent or 0) is unaffected; this is a refusal on evidence, not a\n    79\tguess from the flag.\n    80\t\"\"\"\n    81\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n    82\t\n    83\timport json\n    84\timport os\n    85\timport subprocess\n    86\timport sys\n    87\tfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\n    88\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    89\t\n    90\t# the helper beside adapters/, imported without leaving a __pycache__ there\n    91\tsys.dont_write_bytecode = True\n    92\tsys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent))\n    93\tfrom executor_env import executor_env  # noqa: E402\n    94\t\n    95\tSTATUS_SCHEMA = {\n    96\t    \"type\": \"object\",\n    97\t    \"additionalProperties\": False,\n    98\t    \"required\": [\"status\", \"question\"],\n    99\t    \"properties\": {\n   100\t        \"status\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"done\", \"question\"]},\n   101\t        \"question\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]},\n   102\t    },\n   103\t}\n   104\t\n   105\t# The verify objective (issue #46): a verifier reports findings, not a\n   106\t# commit. additionalProperties: False means the tool cannot hand back a\n   107\t# structured_output shaped like STATUS_SCHEMA's status/question by\n   108\t# accident -- an absent findings key is what cmd_verify treats as\n   109\t# failed, not a lenient default here.\n   110\tVERIFY_SCHEMA = {\n   111\t    \"type\": \"object\",\n   112\t    \"additionalProperties\": False,\n   113\t    \"required\": [\"findings\", \"tests_named\"],\n   114\t    \"properties\": {\n   115\t        \"findings\": {\n   116\t            \"type\": \"array\",\n   117\t            \"items\": {\n   118\t                \"type\": \"object\",\n   119\t                \"additionalProperties\": False,\n   120\t                \"required\": [\"title\", \"specimen\", \"retires\", \"rejection_test\", \"severity\"],\n   121\t                \"properties\": {\n   122\t                    \"title\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1},\n   123\t                    \"specimen\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1},\n   124\t                    \"retires\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1},\n   125\t                    \"rejection_test\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1},\n   126\t                    \"severity\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1},\n   127\t                },\n   128\t            },\n   129\t        },\n   130\t        \"tests_named\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}},\n   131\t    },\n   132\t}\n   133\t\n   134\t# The counsel objective (issue #100): a stop is read inside the product\n   135\t# first, before a person. additionalProperties: False for the same reason\n   136\t# as VERIFY_SCHEMA's own -- the tool cannot hand back a differently-shaped\n   137\t# structured_output by accident.\n   138\tCOUNSEL_SCHEMA = {\n   139\t    \"type\": \"object\",\n   140\t    \"additionalProperties\": False,\n   141\t    \"required\": [\"class\", \"verdict\", \"citations\", \"proposal\"],\n   142\t    \"properties\": {\n   143\t        \"class\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n   144\t        \"verdict\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"answer\", \"patch\", \"person\"]},\n   145\t        \"citations\": {\n   146\t            \"type\": \"array\",\n   147\t            \"items\": {\n   148\t                \"type\": \"object\",\n   149\t                \"additionalProperties\": False,\n   150\t                \"required\": [\"kind\", \"path\", \"symbol\", \"ruling_id\"],\n   151\t                \"properties\": {\n   152\t                    \"kind\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"instruction\", \"mechanism\", \"guard\"]},\n   153\t                    \"path\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]},\n   154\t                    \"symbol\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]},\n   155\t                    \"ruling_id\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]},\n   156\t                },\n   157\t            },\n   158\t        },\n   159\t        \"proposal\": {\n   160\t            \"type\": \"object\",\n   161\t            \"additionalProperties\": False,\n   162\t            \"required\": [\"ruling_text\", \"patch\", \"question\", \"issue\"],\n   163\t            \"properties\": {\n   164\t                \"ruling_text\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]},\n   165\t                \"patch\": {\n   166\t                    \"type\": [\"object\", \"null\"],\n   167\t                    \"additionalProperties\": False,\n   168\t                    \"required\": [\"file\", \"symbol\", \"rejection_test\", \"diff\"],\n   169\t                    \"properties\": {\n   170\t                        \"file\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1},\n   171\t                        \"symbol\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1},\n   172\t                        \"rejection_test\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1},\n   173\t                        \"diff\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1},\n   174\t                    },\n   175\t                },\n   176\t                \"question\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]},\n   177\t                # issue #175: the fourth proposal shape, for a \"patch\" or\n   178\t                # \"person\" verdict whose remedy is better filed as an item\n   179\t                # than shipped as a diff or asked as a bare question.\n   180\t                \"issue\": {\n   181\t                    \"type\": [\"object\", \"null\"],\n   182\t                    \"additionalProperties\": False,\n   183\t                    \"required\": [\"title\", \"body\"],\n   184\t                    \"properties\": {\n   185\t                        \"title\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1},\n   186\t                        \"body\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1},\n   187\t                    },\n   188\t                },\n   189\t            },\n   190\t        },\n   191\t    },\n   192\t}\n   193\t\n   194\t\n   195\tdef read_text(path_env: str) -> str:\n   196\t    path = os.environ.get(path_env)\n   197\t    if not path:\n   198\t        return \"\"\n   199\t    p = Path(path)\n   200\t    return p.read_text() if p.is_file() else \"\"\n   201\t\n   202\t\n   203\tdef describe_file(path: str, text: str, diff_like: bool) -> str:\n   204\t    \"\"\"Path, byte count, line count, and (for a diff) files touched --\n   205\t    named in the instruction instead of inlining the file's own text, so\n   206\t    the instruction stays a small fixed size whatever the file's size\n   207\t    (issue #86: a 27,367-line deletion diff inlined whole exceeded a\n   208\t    judge's input ceiling -- codex's, on the specimen that surfaced it).\n   209\t    Files touched counts unified-diff file headers (`diff --git a/...\n   210\t    b/...`), the shape `git diff` produces.\"\"\"\n   211\t    size = Path(path).stat().st_size\n   212\t    lines = text.count(\"\\n\") + (1 if text and not text.endswith(\"\\n\") else 0)\n   213\t    if not diff_like:\n   214\t        return f\"`{path}` ({size} bytes, {lines} lines)\"\n   215\t    files = sum(1 for l in text.splitlines() if l.startswith(\"diff --git \"))\n   216\t    return f\"`{path}` ({size} bytes, {lines} lines, {files} files touched)\"\n   217\t\n   218\t\n   219\tdef spec_sections() -> list[str]:\n   220\t    \"\"\"The spec's Problem, Claims, and Criteria sections verbatim -- what\n   221\t    both build and verify need to see, in the shape the spec contract\n   222\t    (not this adapter) already gives them.\"\"\"\n   223\t    spec_dir = Path(os.environ[\"ATTAVO_SPEC_DIR\"])\n   224\t    lines = (spec_dir / \"spec.md\").read_text().splitlines()\n   225\t    idx = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith(\"## \")]\n   226\t    headings = {lines[i].strip(): i for i in idx}\n   227\t    bounds = sorted(idx) + [len(lines)]\n   228\t\n   229\t    def section(heading: str) -> str:\n   230\t        start = headings[heading]\n   231\t        end = bounds[bounds.index(start) + 1] if start in bounds else len(lines)\n   232\t        return \"\\n\".join(lines[start:end]).strip()\n   233\t\n   234\t    return [section(\"## Problem\"), section(\"## Claims\"), section(\"## Criteria\")]\n   235\t\n   236\t\n   237\tdef stub_note() -> str | None:\n   238\t    \"\"\"None when ATTAVO_SPEC_DIR carries no stub/; else the sentence\n   239\t    naming what a stub is (issue #90, closed by #93). The stub is\n   240\t    evidence -- a criterion it satisfies trivially is weak -- but twice\n   241\t    the judge reported\n   242\t    a built tree as failing to match its stub as if the stub were the\n   243\t    intended change (tenant zero #664, #644): one sentence of vocabulary\n   244\t    was missing, not a smarter judge or a dropped stub.\"\"\"\n   245\t    stub_dir = Path(os.environ[\"ATTAVO_SPEC_DIR\"]) / \"stub\"\n   246\t    if not stub_dir.is_dir():\n   247\t        return None\n   248\t    return (\n   249\t        f\"## The stub at `{stub_dir}`\\n\\n\"\n   250\t        \"The stub is the fixture the acceptance criteria were shown to \"\n   251\t        \"pass against; it is not the intended change. A difference \"\n   252\t        \"between the built tree and the stub is not a finding: a \"\n   253\t        \"criterion the stub satisfies trivially is.\")\n   254\t\n   255\t\n   256\tdef build_instruction() -> str:\n   257\t    parts = list(spec_sections())\n   258\t\n   259\t    rulings = read_text(\"ATTAVO_RULINGS\")\n   260\t    if rulings.strip():\n   261\t        parts.append(\"## Rulings\\n\\n\" + rulings.strip())\n   262\t\n   263\t    feedback_path = os.environ.get(\"ATTAVO_FEEDBACK\")\n   264\t    feedback = read_text(\"ATTAVO_FEEDBACK\")\n   265\t    if feedback.strip():\n   266\t        parts.append(\n   267\t            \"## Feedback from the previous attempt\\n\\n\"\n   268\t            f\"The feedback is at {describe_file(feedback_path, feedback, diff_like=False)}. \"\n   269\t            \"It is not inlined here: read it yourself with your own tools \"\n   270\t            \"before continuing.\")\n   271\t\n   272\t    parts.append(\n   273\t        \"commit your work on the current branch; if you cannot proceed \"\n   274\t        \"without a decision that changes the criteria, do not guess: \"\n   275\t        \"answer with status question\")\n   276\t\n   277\t    test_command = os.environ.get(\"ATTAVO_TEST_COMMAND\")\n   278\t    if test_command:\n   279\t        bound = os.environ.get(\"ATTAVO_TEST_TIMEOUT_S\")\n   280\t        parts.append(\n   281\t            f\"to run tests while you work, run `{test_command}`: it runs the tests \"\n   282\t            \"selected for the files you have changed\"\n   283\t            + (f\" and stops at {bound} s\" if bound else \"\")\n   284\t            + \". Do not run the whole test suite or any whole-tree check yourself: \"\n   285\t            \"after you commit, the gates are run for you and any failure is \"\n   286\t            \"returned to you on the next iteration\")\n   287\t\n   288\t    return \"\\n\\n\".join(parts)\n   289\t\n   290\t\n   291\tdef verify_instruction() -> str:\n   292\t    parts = list(spec_sections())\n   293\t\n   294\t    note = stub_note()\n   295\t    if note:\n   296\t        parts.append(note)\n   297\t\n   298\t    diff_path = os.environ.get(\"ATTAVO_DIFF\")\n   299\t    diff = read_text(\"ATTAVO_DIFF\")\n   300\t    if diff.strip():\n   301\t        parts.append(\n   302\t            \"## Diff since the approved spec\\n\\n\"\n   303\t            f\"The diff is at {describe_file(diff_path, diff, diff_like=True)}. \"\n   304\t            \"It is not inlined here: read it yourself with your own tools \"\n   305\t            \"before judging it.\")\n   306\t    else:\n   307\t        parts.append(\"## Diff since the approved spec\\n\\n(the diff is empty)\")\n   308\t\n   309\t    build_record_path = os.environ.get(\"ATTAVO_BUILD_RECORD\")\n   310\t    build_record = read_text(\"ATTAVO_BUILD_RECORD\")\n   311\t    if build_record.strip():\n   312\t        parts.append(\n   313\t            \"## The build record\\n\\n\"\n   314\t            f\"The build record is at {describe_file(build_record_path, build_record, diff_like=False)}. \"\n   315\t            \"Read it yourself with your own tools.\")\n   316\t\n   317\t    parts.append(\n   318\t        \"you are verifying a completed build, not building: make no edits, \"\n   319\t        \"write no files, commit nothing. Read the diff named above against \"\n   320\t        \"the criteria and name what the criteria do not assert but the diff \"\n   321\t        \"should still be judged on, and name the tests that would assert \"\n   322\t        \"it if they existed. A spec whose approval commit does not \"\n   323\t        \"describe the working tree the build produced is itself a \"\n   324\t        \"finding: the diff is judged against what was approved, and a \"\n   325\t        \"divergence between them is reportable rather than assumed \"\n   326\t        \"away. Report each as a finding: title, specimen (the file or \"\n   327\t        \"commit the finding is about), retires (what having this \"\n   328\t        \"finding on record replaces or closes -- every finding must \"\n   329\t        \"carry one, or it is refused unfiled), rejection_test (the test \"\n   330\t        \"that would catch a regression of it), and severity. Severity \"\n   331\t        \"is derived rather than judged: the version, counter, \"\n   332\t        \"condition, or state change that flips a finding from harmless \"\n   333\t        \"to blocking; an adjective is not a severity. An empty \"\n   334\t        \"findings list means you looked and found nothing to report, not \"\n   335\t        \"that you did not look.\")\n   336\t    return \"\\n\\n\".join(parts)\n   337\t\n   338\t\n   339\tdef counsel_instruction() -> str:\n   340\t    \"\"\"Issue #100 (extended by issue #175): a stop is read inside the\n   341\t    product first, before a person. The record, its log, the diff, the\n   342\t    forge's checks, the item's graph, the tenant manifest, and this\n   343\t    product's own root are all handed by path -- named in the instruction\n   344\t    instead of inlined, the same discipline verify_instruction already\n   345\t    applies to the diff (issue #86), so this instruction's own size stays\n   346\t    fixed whatever the record, log, diff, checks, or graph's size.\"\"\"\n   347\t    parts = list(spec_sections())\n   348\t\n   349\t    rulings = read_text(\"ATTAVO_RULINGS\")\n   350\t    if rulings.strip():\n   351\t        parts.append(\"## Rulings\\n\\n\" + rulings.strip())\n   352\t\n   353\t    note = stub_note()\n   354\t    if note:\n   355\t        parts.append(note)\n   356\t\n   357\t    record_path = os.environ.get(\"ATTAVO_COUNSEL_RECORD\")\n   358\t    record_text = read_text(\"ATTAVO_COUNSEL_RECORD\")\n   359\t    if record_text.strip():\n   360\t        parts.append(\n   361\t            \"## The stage record\\n\\n\"\n   362\t            f\"The record is at {describe_file(record_path, record_text, diff_like=False)}. \"\n   363\t            \"Read it yourself with your own tools.\")\n   364\t\n   365\t    log_path = os.environ.get(\"ATTAVO_COUNSEL_LOG\")\n   366\t    log_text = read_text(\"ATTAVO_COUNSEL_LOG\")\n   367\t    if log_text.strip():\n   368\t        parts.append(\n   369\t            \"## The record's log\\n\\n\"\n   370\t            f\"The log is at {describe_file(log_path, log_text, diff_like=False)}. \"\n   371\t            \"Read it yourself with your own tools.\")\n   372\t\n   373\t    diff_path = os.environ.get(\"ATTAVO_COUNSEL_DIFF\")\n   374\t    diff_text = read_text(\"ATTAVO_COUNSEL_DIFF\")\n   375\t    if diff_text.strip():\n   376\t        parts.append(\n   377\t            \"## The item's diff since approval\\n\\n\"\n   378\t            f\"The diff is at {describe_file(diff_path, diff_text, diff_like=True)}. \"\n   379\t            \"Read it yourself with your own tools.\")\n   380\t\n   381\t    # issue #175: the forge in the evidence set. ATTAVO_COUNSEL_CHECKS is\n   382\t    # always written, a JSON {read, reason, checks} envelope -- read false\n   383\t    # names the missing manifest key rather than leaving the section out,\n   384\t    # since an unread forge must never be mistaken for a green one.\n   385\t    checks_path = os.environ.get(\"ATTAVO_COUNSEL_CHECKS\")\n   386\t    checks_text = read_text(\"ATTAVO_COUNSEL_CHECKS\")\n   387\t    if checks_text.strip():\n   388\t        parts.append(\n   389\t            \"## The forge's checks on this stop's sha\\n\\n\"\n   390\t            f\"The checks are at {describe_file(checks_path, checks_text, diff_like=False)}: \"\n   391\t            \"a JSON object -- read: false means the forge was not read at \"\n   392\t            \"all (reason names the missing manifest key; treat this as \"\n   393\t            \"unknown, never as green) -- read: true carries one entry per \"\n   394\t            \"check, each naming, for a check that did not succeed, the \"\n   395\t            \"path of its own failed-step log. Read the failing check's \"\n   396\t            \"log before answering about the forge; a remedy that depends \"\n   397\t            \"on the forge's state cites the check and its log line.\")\n   398\t\n   399\t    # issue #175: the graph in the evidence set -- the default branch's\n   400\t    # own log since this item's branch point, this branch's own commits,\n   401\t    # the markers and records present at the stop's sha, and the check\n   402\t    # runs on the last three shas, so \"the checks are on the record\n   403\t    # commit, not the code commit\" is readable without a terminal.\n   404\t    graph_path = os.environ.get(\"ATTAVO_COUNSEL_GRAPH\")\n   405\t    graph_text = read_text(\"ATTAVO_COUNSEL_GRAPH\")\n   406\t    if graph_text.